# TYJC — environment variables.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. It is the one .env* file .gitignore lets through, so
# it must never contain a real value. Copy it to .env for local work; in
# production these are set in the Vercel dashboard (Project -> Settings ->
# Environment Variables), never in the repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY  —  PF-11, required by /api/send-card (RG-06 / US-06)
#
# Resend -> API Keys -> Create API Key. "Sending access" is enough; the endpoint
# only sends. Paste it into Vercel and redeploy — there is no code change.
#
# WITHOUT IT: /api/send-card answers 503 with a plain English message and the
# browser tells the buyer the card is still on screen. Nothing breaks, nothing
# is silently dropped, and no card is lost. That is the deliberate latent state.
#
# SECRET. Whoever holds this key can send email as the domain. Do not paste it
# into chat, a document, or a commit. If it leaks: revoke it in Resend and issue
# a new one — fast and free.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The same key is what switches on /api/waitlist (RG-10 / US-10): the
# post-purchase question and the step-2 waiting list. There is nothing extra to
# create — one key, two endpoints. WITHOUT IT: /api/waitlist answers 503, the
# browser says the list is not switched on yet, and NO waitlist_joined event is
# emitted, so the validation panel reports an honest zero instead of a fake
# capture. H2.2 (>= 40% of buyers on the waiting list) cannot be measured at all
# until this key is set.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FEEDBACK_TO  —  optional. Where the one-question feedback notification lands
# (RG-10). There is no database in the MVP, so the founder's inbox is the store.
# Defaults to contact@lessriskmoregrowth.com when unset. The feedback carries no
# email address and cannot be joined back to a buyer — that is deliberate, see
# the header of api/waitlist.js.
FEEDBACK_TO=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE_URL  —  optional. The base URL the emailed card links back to
# (US-06 AC2: the eight fields AND the way back). Defaults to
# https://lessriskmoregrowth.com when unset. Set it on a preview deployment so
# the link points at the preview instead of production.
SITE_URL=
